---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { scenes } from '../../../config/images';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import ChartGrammar from '../../../components/ChartGrammar.astro';
import HouseWheel from '../../../components/HouseWheel.astro';
import { houses } from '../../../data/houses';
const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Explore Astrology', href: '/explore/' },
  { label: 'The 12 Houses', href: '/explore/houses/' },
];
const groups = ['Angular', 'Succedent', 'Cadent'] as const;
---

<BaseLayout title="The 12 Houses: areas of experience" description="The twelve houses describe areas of life and experience. Learn what each house covers, why birth time matters, and why a house means more in relation to the planets and signs within it." path="/explore/houses/" breadcrumbs={crumbs}>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
  <section class="hero hero--split">
    <div class="container">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Explore Astrology</p>
        <h1>The houses answer: where does it happen?</h1>
        <p class="lede">Houses describe areas of experience. They move astrology from general symbolism into the arenas of a life, and their structure depends on birth time and the house system being used.</p>
      </div>
      <img class="hero__img" src={scenes.houses.src} srcset={scenes.houses.srcset} sizes="100vw" alt={scenes.houses.alt} width={scenes.houses.width} height={scenes.houses.height} fetchpriority="high" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <ChartGrammar active="house" />
      <div class="prose flow">
        <h2>Houses are spatial</h2>
        <p>A house tells us <em>where</em> a chart function is operating, not by itself what will happen there. The Ascendant anchors the house structure, while the four angles establish the chart's primary axes.</p>
      </div>
      <HouseWheel />
      <div class="prose flow">
        <p>This is also why birth time matters. If the Ascendant changes, the house structure can change. When the time is uncertain, a careful astrologer should say what is solid and what is not.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose flow">
        <h2>Learn the houses by how they relate to the angles</h2>
        <p>Numerical order is useful, but angularity gives another way to see the system. The groups below are traditional structural categories, not guarantees about what will happen in a house.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="house-groups">
        {groups.map((group) => (
          <section class="house-group">
            <h2>{group}</h2>
            <div class="house-group__grid">
              {houses.filter((h) => h.angularity === group).map((h) => (
                <a class="house-link" href={`/explore/houses/${h.slug}/`}>
                  <span class="house-link__number">{h.number}</span>
                  <span><strong>{h.name}</strong><small>{h.covers[0]}</small></span>
                </a>
              ))}
            </div>
          </section>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="prose">Go next to <a href="/explore/angles/">the four angles</a> or compare <a href="/explore/house-systems/">house systems</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .house-groups { display: grid; gap: var(--space-8); margin-top: var(--space-8); }
  .house-group__grid { display: grid; gap: var(--space-3); }
  .house-link { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: var(--space-4); align-items: center; padding: var(--space-4); border: 1px solid var(--border-color, currentColor); border-radius: var(--radius-lg, 1rem); text-decoration: none; }
  .house-link__number { display: grid; width: 2.75rem; height: 2.75rem; place-items: center; border: 1px solid currentColor; border-radius: 50%; font-weight: 700; }
  .house-link strong, .house-link small { display: block; }
  .house-link small { margin-top: var(--space-1); }
  @media (min-width: 768px) { .house-group__grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
</style>
